Repository: https://github.com/LaurenzV/hayro (crate hayro-jbig2)
Base: ea9c81dc70cde40c64205986fdcfcd481fe934d8
Fork: https://github.com/close2/hayro

The base is hayro-jbig2 0.3.1: upstream tags the commit `hayro-jbig2-v0.3.1`, the published
crate's `.cargo_vcs_info.json` names it, and its `src/` is byte for byte the published one. The
root Cargo.toml pins the three hayro codecs to upstream's repository at that commit (ADR 1714). The
paths below are the repository's, so the patch applies at its root with `git apply`. The owner
applies this to the fork on that base, pushes, and moves the three stanzas to the fork at the
pushed commit; `tools/state.sh main-checkout` lists it until then.

ITU-T T.88 Annex H.2's test sequence for the arithmetic coder, as a unit test of hayro-jbig2's
arithmetic decoder (ADR 1485). The decoder is `pub(crate)`, so nothing outside the crate can run it
under the single context H.2 uses; the test therefore lives beside it. It decodes H.2's 30 bytes
under one context starting at I(CX) = 0, MPS(CX) = 0 and holds the decoder, before each of the 256
decisions, to Table H.1's row: I(CX), MPS(CX), A, CT and the software-conventions C register (the
decoder follows Annex G), then the decision itself, whose 256 values are also checked against H.2's
32 packed bytes so a transcription slip in either fails. Run at the base revision: passes. Changing
one Qe value (0x5101 to 0x5102) fails it at EC 95, register A. Code only: no behaviour changes.
Independent of the two other hayro-jbig2 patches here. hayro-jpeg2000's copy of the decoder
(`j2c/arithmetic_decoder.rs`) differs from this one only by two `reset` methods on the context.

